# Fund Alpha — .gitignore (E3, 2026-07-22)
#
# Decision: the platform's own bitemporal PIT/vintage system is the
# versioning mechanism for RESEARCH DATA (equity_prices, index_levels,
# etc. all carry as_of_date + source_id already). Git tracks CODE,
# CONFIG, DOCS, and small validated REFERENCE outputs — not the raw
# archive or live databases. Rationale per item:

# Raw document/PDF/zip archive (~5.9GB, permanent but regenerated by the
# harvest_*.py scripts from NGX's own servers if ever lost — not code).
data/archive/

# Daily raw capture snapshots (small individually, grows unbounded daily;
# the research DB is the durable store for anything ingested from these).
data/capture/

# Staged intermediate parse outputs (~97MB, fully regenerable from
# data/archive/ via the parse_*.py / build_*.py scripts — regenerating
# is the correct recovery path, not a git checkout).
data/staging/

# Live research/registry databases — change on every ingest/experiment;
# PIT vintages + the immutable registry ARE their own audit trail.
# Binary diffs of a growing sqlite file provide no real history value.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
